{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Your throat</b> — it is the house of swallowing, that is: you will put a knife in your throat, if you are a man of appetite given to craving, and you will rule over it. And he mentioned bread because it is the essence of the meal, or it is a general term for all foods, as in: \"who gives bread to all flesh\" (Psalms 136:25)."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:15.867255980Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}